  "body": {
   "blocks": [
    [
     {
      "text": "As well as the while statement just introduced, Python uses a few more that we will encounter in this",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "chapter.",
      "mono": false
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "Perhaps the most well-known statement type is the if statement. For example:",
      "mono": false
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "\u003e\u003e\u003e x = int(input(\"Please enter an integer: \"))",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "Please enter an integer: 42",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "\u003e\u003e\u003e if x \u003c 0:",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "...     x = 0",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "...     print('Negative changed to zero')",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "... elif x == 0:",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "...     print('Zero')",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "... elif x == 1:",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "...     print('Single')",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "... else:",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "...     print('More')",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "...",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "More",
      "mono": true
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "There can be zero or more elif parts, and the else part is optional. The keyword \u2018elif\u2019 is short for",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "\u2018else if\u2019, and is useful to avoid excessive indentation. An if \u2026 elif \u2026 elif \u2026 sequence is a substitute",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "for the switch or case statements found in other languages.",
      "mono": false
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "If you\u2019re comparing the same value to several constants, or checking for specific types or attributes, you",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "may also find the match statement useful. For more details see match Statements.",
      "mono": false
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "The for statement in Python differs a bit from what you may be used to in C or Pascal. Rather than",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "always iterating over an arithmetic progression of numbers (like in Pascal), or giving the user the ability",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "to define both the iteration step and halting condition (as C), Python\u2019s for statement iterates over the",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "items of any sequence (a list or a string), in the order that they appear in the sequence. For example (no",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "pun intended):",
      "mono": false
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "\u003e\u003e\u003e # Measure some strings:",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "\u003e\u003e\u003e words = ['cat', 'window', 'defenestrate']",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "\u003e\u003e\u003e for w in words:",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "...     print(w, len(w))",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "...",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "cat 3",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "window 6",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "defenestrate 12",
      "mono": true
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "Code that modifies a collection while iterating over that same collection can be tricky to get right.",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "Instead, it is usually more straight-forward to loop over a copy of the collection or to create a new",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "collection:",
      "mono": false
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "# Create a sample collection",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "users = {'Hans': 'active', '\u00c9l\u00e9onore': 'inactive', '\u666f\u592a\u90ce': 'active'}",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "# Strategy:  Iterate over a copy",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "for user, status in users.copy().items():",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "    if status == 'inactive':",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "        del users[user]",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "# Strategy:  Create a new collection",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "active_users = {}",
